        <id>https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/43709</id>
        <link href="https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/43709"/>
        <updated>2026-04-08T14:56:38.000Z</updated>
        <content type="html"><![CDATA[<img src="https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/7020796?v=4" width="64" height="64" alt=""/><br/>

<h3 dir="auto">Description</h3>
<p dir="auto">Fixed the resultant values listed in the examples of accessing the <code class="notranslate">minutes</code> property of an unbalanced <code class="notranslate">Duration</code>. It will be <code class="notranslate">30</code>, not <code class="notranslate">1</code>, when taking the <code class="notranslate">minutes</code> value of an unbalanced <code class="notranslate">Duration</code> initialised from <code class="notranslate">{ hours: 1, minutes: 30 }</code>.</p>
<h3 dir="auto">Motivation</h3>
<p dir="auto">This was the first of the <code class="notranslate">Duration</code> accessors I read about and I stared at the example for quite a while trying to work out where the <code class="notranslate">1</code> would have come from!</p>
<h3 dir="auto">Additional details</h3>
<p dir="auto">Verified that this is now the correct value by running the expressions in Chrome's console.</p>
]]></content>
